+5.  **Calculate Coverage Fraction ($\alpha$):** For each representative point $x$, calculate the fraction of the pixel covered by the surface. Assuming local planarity, the surface intersects the cone's cross-section (a disk of radius $r_p$) with a straight edge at signed distance $f(x)$ from the center [S1, S3].
